---
import FaqList from "../../components/FaqList.astro";
import InsetText from "../../components/govuk/InsetText.astro";
import AudienceLayout from "../../layouts/AudienceLayout.astro";
---

<AudienceLayout
	title="Social workers"
	lead="Your role in the Personal Education Plan, and how to work with the Virtual School to improve a child's education."
	description="Your part in the PEP, how to refer a child, and how we work together to improve outcomes."
	accent="var(--rvs-audience-social)"
>
	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Your role in the PEP</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		The PEP forms part of the child's care plan. It is a shared responsibility between the social
		worker, the school and the Virtual School, and it should be a live document that reflects the
		child's day-to-day experience.
	</p>
	<p class="govuk-body">As the social worker, you are responsible for:</p>
	<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
		<li>making sure the PEP happens within the statutory timescales</li>
		<li>chairing or attending the PEP meeting, and making sure the child's views are captured</li>
		<li>making sure the PEP links to the wider care plan — health, contact, placement stability</li>
		<li>escalating to the Virtual School when a school is not meeting the child's needs</li>
	</ul>
	<InsetText title="Placement moves and school">
		<p class="govuk-body">
			Tell us as early as possible about a placement move. A rushed school move is the single
			biggest cause of lost school time for children in care, and we can usually prevent it if
			we have notice.
		</p>
	</InsetText>

	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Raising a concern</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		If you think a child's education is at risk — attendance is dropping, a school is not putting
		the PEP provision in place, or an exclusion is being considered — contact the Virtual School
		directly rather than waiting for the next review.
	</p>
	<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
		<li>Email the team: <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:virtualschool@rotherham.gov.uk">virtualschool@rotherham.gov.uk</a></li>
		<li>See <a class="govuk-link" href="/our-team/">our team</a> for the phase lead for your child</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Attendance and exclusions</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		We monitor attendance and exclusion data for every child in care. Where a child is at risk of
		exclusion, we expect to be involved before a decision is made, so that support can be put in
		place instead.
	</p>

	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Post-16 and care leavers</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		Education support does not stop at 16. We work with personal advisers on pathways into
		college, apprenticeships, training and work, and on the financial support available to care
		leavers.
	</p>

	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Training</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		We run workshops for social workers on writing and reviewing high-quality PEPs. See
		<a class="govuk-link" href="/training-events/">training and events</a> to book.
	</p>

	<FaqList audience="social-workers" />
</AudienceLayout>
